    "redistribute": true,
    "notes": "Collected but NOT published, pending verification. The adapter runs and returns plausible numbers, but coverage differs per metric without a stated reason — housing volume landed five cities, tone a different five, total volume six — which is the shape of intermittent fetch failures being absorbed rather than of a rule about what is measurable. Barcelona and Sevilla also swap rank mid-series, which is not obviously real. News attention is genuinely hard here: \"Valencia\" is also a city in Venezuela and \"Malaga\" one in Colombia, so a plausible-looking series of the wrong city is worse than no series. The history stays in the repository so the question can be settled; nothing reaches the site until it is.\n"
   }
